<Site
  title="About · Ouijit"
  description="Ouijit is built by one person, Prentice Bjerkeseth. Free, open source under AGPL, no account and no telemetry, and the plan is to keep it that way.">
  <main class="compare-content about-content">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      A tool for working with coding agents should protect your focus and your judgement as you get more done
      with it. That is what Ouijit is built for. It gives every task its own worktree and terminal so each
      piece of work can be looked at on its own, and it runs the agents' own CLIs rather than standing in for
      them, because the command line is where their tooling moves fastest.
    </p>
    <p>
      A tool like this also shouldn't need an account, a subscription, or a company behind it. Ouijit is free
      and open source under AGPL-3.0, with no telemetry. If it ever charges for something, that will be a
      feature with a running cost of its own, like hosted environments or sync.
    </p>
    <p>
      Many tools like this are raising venture money, getting acquired, or shutting down. I build Ouijit alone
      and intend to keep it that way.
    </p>
    <p class="about-sign"><a href="https://github.com/pbjer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Prentice Bjerkeseth</a></p>
  </main>
</Site>
